  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\nDense fog, with coverage ranging from areas to widespread, is \ndeveloping across Northwest OH early this morning. Patchier\ndense fog is also developing across some river valleys farther\neast-southeast across North Central Ohio. Will continue to\nmonitor the coverage of the fog and issue any additional\nadvisories or statements as needed early this morning.\n\nOutside of nightly fog and frost potential, the forecast remains\nextremely tranquil and seasonable through early next week. Low\ntemperatures may be slightly chillier tonight/Thursday morning,\nleading to greater frost potential. Thursday night trends a few\ndegrees milder with lesser frost potential. Friday night/early \nSaturday will trend several degrees cooler, and look to feature\nmore widespread frost potential, including in portions of the \narea where the growing season hasn't been ended yet. \n\nA front is expected to cross Tuesday or Tuesday night, with\npotential for just a bit of rain along or behind the front late\nTuesday into Wednesday. Otherwise, the forecast is dry for the\nduration. One item to monitor is the potential for a few lake-\nenhanced sprinkles late Thursday into early Friday as a trough\naxis pushes across Lake Erie, though the odds of any measurable\nrain with that feature appear too low for a forecast mention.",
